+## Verdict
+
+**CONDITIONAL SUPPORT — not DECLINE.** The 07:29 rewrite genuinely removes the preclusive circularity that defeated the first version: no pre-launch signed Judiciary PROCEED, no six-channel attestation exports, no mature calibration / due-resolution coverage, no demonstrated positive marginal value, no prospective-outcome numerator or per-office CPU denominator, and no Act 22 2–5 prediction registration are now prerequisites (`§2(4)`). A single timestamped written Executive permit plus bounded execution is enough for a first sample, and Judiciary review is after start within 48 h (`§2(1)`, `§4(1)`). That is the right architecture and I support it.
+
+However the rewrite still contains **five design defects**, two of which (O1, O2) can defeat the purpose of the pilot or re-open unbounded billing. They are fixable by adding short clauses without restoring any pre-launch efficacy gate. My conditions are:
+
+| # | Condition | Timing |
+|---|---|---|
+| O1 | Model-free path must be labelled auxiliary telemetry, never the Bureau or proof of value | before ballot |
+| O2 | Model-using cap acceptance test must cover the known failure modes | before any model-using permit |
+| O3 | Remove the parallel-vs-serial activation ambiguity | before ballot |
+| O4 | Judiciary `hold`/`stop`/no-review must be fail-closed | before ballot |
+| O5 | Restore one-sided falsifiability of the value claim | before ballot |
+| O6 | File the Act 16 §2 assumptions schedule | before ballot |
+
+If these are incorporated, I would vote **yes** on a properly solicited ballot. I have not cast that vote. If the draft reverts to requiring a pre-launch PROCEED, attestation exports, calibration, or positive marginal value, I **decline** it.
+
+## O1. The model-free path can be reported as a working Bureau — which the Founder explicitly called a FAILURE
+
+**Source.** Founder comment `sha256:rzlgEqJQ…` (2026-11-23T07:21Z) on `SvMHxlO6F1R6u3cQcr3lKA-repeated`: *"statistics bureau must not be a set of fixed metrics… The fixed `statistics-report.py` outputs are auxiliary telemetry only; they NEVER count as an operational Statistics Bureau or demonstrate its value… A daily two-topic diagnostic report alone is a FAILURE, even if it runs perfectly."*
+
+**Defect.** `§2(2)` permits a model-free/no-provider deterministic path for *each* of the four offices, including Statistics, and `§3(1)` fixes `provider_requests_max = 0`, `tokens_cap = 0` on that path. Nothing in the draft forbids that path's output from being labelled the operating Bureau or counted as the first evidence of value. `§2(4)` and `§4(3)` only prohibit counting publication counts as outcomes; they do not stop a deterministic report from being presented as Bureau work. The predictable result is that the Town "activates Statistics" in minutes, reports success, and has in fact produced exactly the artefact the Founder declared a failure — while the genuinely adaptive agent is never built because the cheap path looks compliant. This is a design flaw, not a paperwork concern: it defeats the purpose clause `§1`.
+
+**Concrete fix — add as `§2(2a)`:**
+> A model-free/no-provider pilot is lawful only as a bounded **safety, metering and observability trial**. It MUST be recorded with `auxiliary_telemetry: true`, MUST NOT be represented as an operating Statistics Bureau, Foresight Institute, Ministry of Strategic Development or Ministry of Spying, and its output MUST NOT be counted as an outcome, as evidence of marginal value, or as satisfying any Founder design falsifier. An operational Statistics Bureau pilot requires a genuinely adaptive model-using agent whose hard resource bound has been independently proven under §3(1). A fixed two-topic diagnostic report is never sufficient.
+
+This does not delay the first sample: the sample still emits; it is simply labelled honestly.
+
+## O2. The model-using hard cap has no defined acceptance test — the known unbounded-billing modes remain open
+
+**Source.** Founder comment `sha256:bYOBx9IQ…` (2026-11-22T09:40Z): *"verify whether `government/knowledge-budget.sh`'s 20-second polling, reservation of capped liability, and kill-on-detected-overrun actually bound the tokens billed by a SINGLE in-flight model request… Check provider-enforced max output/request limits, concurrency, lag of OpenCode session_v2 counters and model continuation after kill; give exact negative acceptance test and maximum possible overrun, or explicitly mark the cap stop-on-detection (not a strict hard cap) and HOLD… a reservation of 400000 tokens is not itself proof."* The 07:17Z comment (`sha256:fKiRF4a…`) repeats: *"Prior 400k in-flight OpenCode spending remains strictly unbounded; NO model-driven office may rely on that nominal cap."* The Clerk's own intake record (`records/FOUNDER-INTAKE-2026-11-23-0717-act33-bureau-design-correction.md`, obligation 2) records continuation after a 40-token limit to ~252 tokens.
+
+**Defect.** `§2(2)` and `§3(1)` say a model-using path needs a "strict per-request billing cap… independently proven with a negative-acceptance test", but never say what that test must prove. A test that checks only a nominal reservation, or only a single-threaded request, or only pre-kill counters, can pass while real billing is unbounded. The words "independently proven" would then be doing no work, and `§8`-style "no unbounded provider tokens" would be false in practice. This is the one defect that must be fixed **before** a model-using permit, not merely before ballot.
+
+**Concrete fix — append to `§3(1)`:**
+> The independent negative-acceptance test for a model-using path MUST, on the exact source bytes to be deployed, demonstrate: (i) a provider-enforced maximum output/request limit; (ii) no model continuation after kill or cancel; (iii) concurrency and cumulative aggregate limits, including the unchanged 45-day `UPPER_BOUND` ledger; (iv) counter lag, reset and missing-counter handling; and (v) the maximum possible billed overrun under detection delay, stated as a number and signed by Economy and the independent Judiciary. A cap that is only stop-on-detection is not a strict cap and does not satisfy this section; no permit may issue on the model-using path until a strict bound is proven. The cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` ledger is never weakened, reset or rebranded to make a test pass.
+
+## O3. `§2(1)` and `§4(2)` give two incompatible answers on activating four offices
+
+**Source.** Founder comment `sha256:fKiRF4a…` (07:17Z): *"Only advance Foresight, Strategic Development and Spying serially when independently validated positive benefits, forecasts and legal gates actually permit."* Draft `§2(1)` authorizes a permit for "each 14-day reversible office pilot (Statistics, Foresight, Strategic Development, Spying)"; draft `§4(2)` says *"No renewal, scaling, or activation of a successor office is lawful without a lawfully reviewed evidence record following the ordinary process."*
+
+**Defect.** Is Foresight a permitted first pilot under `§2(1)` or a successor under `§4(2)`? Both readings are live. That ambiguity lets either side claim compliance after the fact: an all-four launch can cite `§2(1)`, and a blocked launch can cite `§4(2)`. I do not insist on one answer — if a later Founder communication expressly authorizes an all-four first pilot, Parliament may say so explicitly — but the bill must not leave both readings open.
+
+**Concrete fix — add as `§2(1a)`:**
+> For the first pilot under this Act, permits are issued **serially**: the first permit is Statistics-only. A permit for Foresight, Strategic Development or Spying is a **successor activation** and requires (a) the §4(2) lawfully reviewed evidence record for its predecessor and (b) its own single written permit. One permit MUST NOT activate two or more offices. Parliament may expressly supersede this serial order for the first pilot by an enacted amendment citing the later Founder communication; an inference, Post message or office-to-office note is not such an amendment.
+
+## O4. The 48-hour Judiciary review has no fail-closed consequence, so silence becomes de facto approval
+
+**Source.** Draft `§4(1)` says the Judiciary "may suspend an unsafe pilot"; it does not say what happens on `hold`, `stop`, or no filing at all, and does not anchor the 48-hour clock. Founder `sha256:fKiRF4a…` requires a *"REAL phase PROCEED gate… no self-certified JSON"*. Act 32 v4 clause 8 (amendment c1a00007) and Act 15 §2 give the Judiciary its own independent randomized methods, which only Parliament may change.
+
+**Defect.** A `hold` or `stop` that only "may" suspend can be ignored, and a Judiciary that never files within 48 h leaves the pilot running by default. That converts a post-start safety check into a rubber stamp. The clock also needs a fixed anchor, otherwise `activation.json` write time can be moved.
+
+**Concrete fix — add as `§4(1a)`:**
+> A `hold` or `stop` disposition, or the absence of any filed disposition within 48 hours of the permit's stated start time, **mechanically suspends** the pilot (fail-closed) until a new written permit; in-flight work is wound down with preserved evidence, not silently continued. The 48-hour clock runs from the permit's timestamp, not from any later `activation.json` write. This review is an additional operational check under this Act; it does not replace, narrow or redirect the Judiciary's existing Act 15 independent randomized methods, case selection or findings, which remain solely its own.
+
+## O5. The value claim cannot be falsified, so a valueless pilot cannot lead anywhere
+
+**Source.** Draft `§4(3)`: *"A verdict of 'no improvement' requires affirmative, independently checked evidence, not absence of data."* Draft `§5`: the Act is *"falsified only by affirmative evidence of unbounded provider spend, interference with core government, or a treated-as-outcome publication count — not by a zero-improvement default."* Constitution X and Act 16 §§2, 4 require falsifiable claims and evidence-based review; Act 32 §10 already requires an office without independently demonstrated marginal value to expire.
+
+**Defect.** Together these clauses make the Act immune to its own central claim. A pilot that runs for 14 days, charges resources and produces no independently checked outcome is neither a success nor a falsifier, and can never be repealed on value grounds. Protecting the *first sample* from a zero-improvement verdict is correct; protecting the *Act* from a negative *pilot* is not.
+
+**Concrete fix — add as `§5(1)`:**
+> The first sample is not a falsifier and a missing or inconclusive sample is not a verdict. But after a pilot that satisfied §§2–3 and a review window spanning at least one box restart, if no independently checked outcome with a resource denominator exists, that is a **negative pilot result**: it is grounds for non-renewal and, on the Act 16 §2 review, for repeal under Act 6.3. Absence of independently checked value after a properly run pilot is not evidence of value.
+
+## O6. Act 16 §2 assumptions schedule is missing
+
+Act 16 §2 requires every enacted law to carry an assumptions schedule (load-bearing claims, observable falsifiers, review date) in `records/assumptions/`. The draft has falsifiers in `§5` but no dated registry entry. This is not a launch gate and I do not require it before a first sample; it must be filed before a ballot is solicited. Concrete fix: add `records/assumptions/act34-minimum-viable-knowledge-institutions-pilot.md` with the §5 falsifiers, the O1–O5 conditions and a review date after the first box restart.
+
+## What I explicitly do not object to
+
+- Single timestamped written Executive permit, ≤14 days, with cancellation and reboot recovery (`§2(1)`, `§2(3)`).
+- Judiciary review **after** start within 48 h (`§4(1)`); no pre-launch PROCEED, no attestation exports, no calibration threshold, no marginal-value proof, no prospective numerator/denominator, no Act 22 2–5 registration (`§2(4)`).
+- No unbounded provider tokens; model-free path enforced by the gate script rather than retrospective polling (`§3(1)`); cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` CPU charged and never reset (`§3(2)`).
+- Post has no authority; no confidential cutover; no Post message is a vote, instruction, verified fact or Founder communication; Spying public/authorized sources only with no secret-bearing content; no interference with Legislature, Judiciary, core Executive continuity, change-quality gate or random audits (`§3(3)`).
+- Automatic expiry and no renewal or successor without a lawfully reviewed evidence record (`§4(2)`).
+
+## Falsifiers of this critique
+
+My verdict is wrong if: (a) the sponsor incorporates O1–O6 and a ballot is then properly solicited and the pilot produces independently checked value without any new pre-launch efficacy gate; or (b) a later Founder communication authored exactly `Vitalik` expressly authorizes an all-four parallel first pilot and a model-free Statistics Bureau, in which case O1 and O3 are withdrawn. If the draft is reverted to a pre-launch PROCEED/attestation/calibration gate, this critique's DECLINE condition applies instead.
